#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# fourier_cos_transform

#% text
# `fourier_cos_transform(f, t, w)` gives the cosine transform `sqrt(2/pi) integrate(f*cos(w*t), [t, 0, inf])` of `f`, for `w > 0`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The integral is taken with `w > 0`; when `integrate` finds no value, the Laplace transform on the imaginary axis gives it.

#% item
# `g(t)/t` with `g(0) = 0` gives the integral of the sine transform of `g` from `w` to `inf`.

#% item
# `fourier_parameters: [a, b]` gives `2 sqrt(abs(b)/(2 pi)^(1 - a)) integrate(f*cos(b*w*t), [t, 0, inf])`.

#% item
# The transform is its own inverse.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
fourier_cos_transform(exp(-t), t, w)
#% output
#= 2^(1/2)*(pi^-1)^(1/2)/(1 + w^2)

#% cell
fourier_cos_transform(1/(1 + t^2), t, w)
#% output
#= (1/2)*2^(1/2)*exp(-w)*pi^(1/2)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
fourier_cos_transform(exp(-t^2), t, w)
#% output
#= (1/2)*2^(1/2)*exp((-1/4)*w^2)

#% cell
fourier_cos_transform(1/sqrt(t), t, w)
#% output
#= w^(-1/2)

#% cell
fourier_cos_transform(unit_box(t - 1/2), t, w)
#% output
#= 2^(1/2)*(pi^-1)^(1/2)*sinc(w)

#% cell
fourier_cos_transform(sin(t)*exp(-t)/t, t, w)
#% output
#= (-1/4)*(-pi^(1/2) + 2*atan((1/2)*w^2)/pi^(1/2))*2^(1/2)

#% subsection
# Options

#% cell
fourier_cos_transform(1/sqrt(t), t, w, fourier_parameters: [1, 2*pi])
#% output
#= 2^(1/2)*pi^(1/2)/w^(1/2)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `inverse_fourier_cos_transform`, `fourier_sin_transform`, `fourier_transform`
